sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch09-02> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Sea-urchin eggs reared in lime-free sea-water develop into apparently healthy larvae that lack the calcareous skeletal rods, and the long larval arms normally supported by those rods are suppressed; the organism can live without the material of its skeleton.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sea-urchin larvae reared without lime develop healthily but lack skeletal rods and arms";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter IX, “On Concretions, Spicules, and Spicular Skeletons”; topic “Development without skeletal material”. Scope: echinoid pluteus larvae (and by extension skeleton-forming organisms deprived of skeletal material)"
}
